Step 3: What You Do in the DBaaS GUI

1. After your initial ADT build completes in a region, grab the public IPs of your init webservers (e.g., if you built 2 or 3 init webservers, you have 2 or 3 public IPs).
2. Whitelist only those init public IPs in your DBaaS firewall GUI once.
3. Because every init webserver has its own direct route to the DBaaS (using its own whitelisted public IP) and every autoscaled webserver routes through those init servers, you never need to touch the DBaaS firewall when autoscaling up or down.
